{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0","id":1077188,"title":"On Non-Iremite Mummies (v 4.0)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T13:47:48-07:00","id":1077188,"title":"On Non-Iremite Mummies (v 4.0)","content":"My last attempt to garner some interest in the idea of Non-Iremite Arisen (based on the conceit that Sekhem is a universal constant and thus the Rite of Return could conceivably happen anywhere) met with some modest success, but by and large, the consensus seems that any new types of mummy should be their own thing, separate from the concepts of the Arisen. So, now that the Dark Ages Companion is out (specifically the chapter on Cleopatra's Egypt, rich as it is with material on other immortal beings), I figured I'd give it another try along those lines.<br /> <br /> The first point of order: Should there be generic rules for these second string mummies, with any relevant names/mechanics altered to fit the origin culture; OR, should mummy types be built from the ground up for every culture, each type being its own special supernatural snowflake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:57:47-07:00","id":1077194,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think non-Iremite mummies could be treated as either immortals or CoD Horrors. On a related note, would they also draw on Sekhem as an animating power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:39:10-07:00","id":1077289,"title":"","content":"Ideally, yes, but technically so is everything else in existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:22:38-07:00","id":1077322,"title":"","content":"I realise that this isn't strictly related, but where is the Dark Ages Companion? I looked on DrivethruRPG and couldn't find it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to the point, I think the most important things are,firstly, don't have too many mummies. The rite took the death of thousands and the resources of an empire to pull off, and on a meta level it takes away the specialness of Irem if every backwater fiefdom was building its own mummies. I would argue that, at most, one major &quot;type&quot; of Arisen per continent is reasonable.<br /> <br /> Secondly, make the new mummies unique. Irem's use of the Rite was very much based on their ideologies, beliefs and culture, and another culture's use should produce something radically different. (also, if you just want the arisen but ,I dunno, Incan themed you can just refluff the terms in Mummy and use it as is anyway.). I would say that any non-Iremite mummies should be at least as different to the arisen as the Decived are.<br /> <br /> (A headcanon of mine is that the ritual was done at least one other time, in a city called Dis but using the Strix instead of the Judges and creating the first vampires (who are also deathless creatures that feed on life to avoid descending to the underworld). While that's obviously not canon, I would argue that any use of the ritual should be at least potentially as impressive in its effects on the world. No matter where you are, the Rite of Return isn't something you do casually or without major consequences)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:33:59-07:00","id":1077354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1077322#post1077322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realise that this isn't strictly related, but where is the Dark Ages Companion? I looked on DrivethruRPG and couldn't find it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, I forgot, it's only been released to certain backers from the first book's Kickstarter. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:27:38-07:00","id":1077386,"title":"","content":"Seconding uniqueness. Maybe this could double as a Immortals 2e as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:43:45-07:00","id":1077392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0#post1077188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first point of order: Should there be generic rules for these second string mummies, with any relevant names/mechanics altered to fit the origin culture; OR, should mummy types be built from the ground up for every culture, each type being its own special supernatural snowflake?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm largely of the opinion that the Arisen as they are aren't an optimal design for what the Judges or Shan'iatu wanted - it seems to me that the Judges would be wanting Sekhem 10 horrors up 24/7 - the Shan'iatu might want them to sleep sometimes, if only to carry relics to Duat when they do, but would prefer nary a hint of memory of their former lives. They don't get that - such pure Sekhem demands significant recharge, while even the Rite can't stop memory trickling back.<br /> <br /> Ergo, there are trade-offs built into the nature of Sekhem - design constraints that even the Shan'iatu were stuck with. Decide what those are going to be in your setting - eg, Sekhem always drains out in something akin to the Descent - and make sure every &quot;design&quot; of mummy is stuck with them to at least the same degree. But let the rest be shaped by culture.<br /> <br /> Irem produced a few hundred mummies. No one else should have anything like that number - even a dozen might be the second-highest tally.<br /> <br /> Don't be ashamed to adapt Curse mechanics to represent them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:47:15-07:00","id":1077393,"title":"","content":"I do think non-Iremite Mummies should be something completely different, both from Arisen and from each other. No Rite of Return transplanted into a different culture, or Arisen mechanics in a different flesh. Honestly, a somewhat semantic part of me gets annoyed that this conversation happens in the &quot;Mummy&quot; sub-forum rather than just in the general Chronicles of Darkness discussion, because I have never heard a satisfactory argument as to why any Mummy not from Irem would be part of this game line. So far as I can tell it's just confusion over the fact that the English language uses the same word, &quot;Mummy&quot;, to describe preserved corpses from a variety of different cultures that were created via different methods for different reasons. There's no meaningful connection between Egyptian, Incan, Aboriginal, and Danish Mummies, to name a few examples. Some were ritual sacrifices, others were prepared as part of that culture's mortuary traditions, and some were criminals being put to death. Supernatural equivalents have similarly little reason to be discussed in relation to one another.<br /> <br /> A single non-Arisen &quot;Mummy&quot; template consequently feels like a gross generalisation, equating all traditions of preserving bodies as both the same regardless of culture and intent, while also treating them as &quot;other&quot; (in that it's not like typical Western burial customs) and thus inherently mystical in a way that reeks of a variant of Orientalism. The only way I can think of to do it satisfactorily, without those unpleasant undertones, would be to toss out any relation to mummified bodies specifically and to instead create a generic Revenant template that can be applied to absolutely any corpse, mummified or not.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh wait, Mummy already has rules for generic Revenant templates. Well, that was easy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:10:37-07:00","id":1077415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1077393#post1077393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think non-Iremite Mummies should be something completely different, both from Arisen and from each other. No Rite of Return transplanted into a different culture, or Arisen mechanics in a different flesh. Honestly, a somewhat semantic part of me gets annoyed that this conversation happens in the &quot;Mummy&quot; sub-forum rather than just in the general Chronicles of Darkness discussion, because I have never heard a satisfactory argument as to why any Mummy not from Irem would be part of this game line. So far as I can tell it's just confusion over the fact that the English language uses the same word, &quot;Mummy&quot;, to describe preserved corpses from a variety of different cultures that were created via different methods for different reasons. There's no meaningful connection between Egyptian, Incan, Aboriginal, and Danish Mummies, to name a few examples. Some were ritual sacrifices, others were prepared as part of that culture's mortuary traditions, and some were criminals being put to death. Supernatural equivalents have similarly little reason to be discussed in relation to one another.<br /> <br /> A single non-Arisen &quot;Mummy&quot; template consequently feels like a gross generalisation, equating all traditions of preserving bodies as both the same regardless of culture and intent, while also treating them as &quot;other&quot; (in that it's not like typical Western burial customs) and thus inherently mystical in a way that reeks of a variant of Orientalism. The only way I can think of to do it satisfactorily, without those unpleasant undertones, would be to toss out any relation to mummified bodies specifically and to instead create a generic Revenant template that can be applied to absolutely any corpse, mummified or not.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh wait, Mummy already has rules for generic Revenant templates. Well, that was easy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly understandable. Still, these discussion do often lead to some decent ideas regarding other critter types, even if they are only tangentally related to the Arisen.<br /> <br /> For instance, I've recently gotten the idea for something that might look like a Rite of Return Mummy to cursory inspection. A Hybrid of Eternals (lives as long as their special-item does) and Soul-Forging Relic makers, with a bit of Sacred Geometry thrown in there. Basic summary is they forge their soul/spirit/whatever into a Relic, then set it up into a kind of proto/knock-off Life Web (with Vestiges and stuff) to accumulate energy/Sekhem. When it is &quot;enough&quot; (voluntary or triggered?), the being awakens to new life. Their powers all basically provoke Descent checks, bleeding off more of their mojo as they exert themselves, until they need to rest and recharge once more.<br /> <br /> They <i>hate</i> Arisen, obviously, since the Iremites are stronger, tougher, can sniff out their sustaining Relic, and destroy it by sending it to the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:34:39-07:00","id":1077586,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is the fourth thread you've made about the same topic and the other threads are still on the front page of this subforum. Please do not make another thread about the same topic, it's poor forum etiquette and will be deleted. If you want to add something new to the topic or revisit the conversation then post in an existing thread. Thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T08:55:52-07:00","id":1077758,"title":"","content":"My apologies, I never intended to do anything to make the moderators break out the red text. This will be the new Master Thread for this topic.<br /> <br /> And in that spirit, here are links to the past threads, should anyone want to re-read them for new ideas:<br /> <br /> First Thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876960-on-non-iremite-mummies\">On Non-Iremite Mummies</a><br /> <br /> Second Thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1022594-on-the-spontaneous-arising-of-non-iremite-mummies\">On the Spontaneous Arising of Non-Iremite Mummies</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1077393#post1077393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think non-Iremite Mummies should be something completely different, both from Arisen and from each other. No Rite of Return transplanted into a different culture, or Arisen mechanics in a different flesh. Honestly, a somewhat semantic part of me gets annoyed that this conversation happens in the &quot;Mummy&quot; sub-forum rather than just in the general Chronicles of Darkness discussion, because I have never heard a satisfactory argument as to why any Mummy not from Irem would be part of this game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only speak for myself, but I included it here because I was hoping to explore the Themes of Mummy (memory, self-discovery, identity, purpose...) in new and different <i>milieus</i>. How might the story of one of the Arisen be different from, say, a bog-man originally sacrificed as an offering to the gods, rather than as a servant? The Arisen are yoked by the Judges, by their Cults (at least, nominally), and by the stars themselves, and are hounded by enemies both familiar (Shuankhsen, Deceived) and worldly (Last Dynasty); whereas our bog-man may only deal with one or two similar factors, or perhaps none of them at all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I can tell it's just confusion over the fact that the English language uses the same word, &quot;Mummy&quot;, to describe preserved corpses from a variety of different cultures that were created via different methods for different reasons. There's no meaningful connection between Egyptian, Incan, Aboriginal, and Danish Mummies, to name a few examples. Some were ritual sacrifices, others were prepared as part of that culture's mortuary traditions, and some were criminals being put to death. Supernatural equivalents have similarly little reason to be discussed in relation to one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so it seems here that the most major difference between the Arisen and any other potential mummy groups, aside from culture, would be their purpose. The Arisen, one and all, were sacrificed to be servants, not of the gods or even of their cults, but of the Shan'iatu (and yes, the Shan'iatu are possibly divine, but I think it's a whole other thing when the gods you're sacrificed to serve are the ones doing the sacrificing in the first place).<br /> <br /> So these new mummies, beyond any in-game history/backstory we provide them, helps us answer the question of &quot;In the absence of such definitive roles given to them and the leadership/programming of the Judges, how might the Arisen have turned out?&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 04-13-2017, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:37:47-07:00","id":1077976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1077758#post1077758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so it seems here that the most major difference between the Arisen and any other potential mummy groups, aside from culture, would be their purpose. The Arisen, one and all, were sacrificed to be servants, not of the gods or even of their cults, but of the Shan'iatu (and yes, the Shan'iatu are possibly divine, but I think it's a whole other thing when the gods you're sacrificed to serve are the ones doing the sacrificing in the first place).<br /> <br /> So these new mummies, beyond any in-game history/backstory we provide them, helps us answer the question of &quot;In the absence of such definitive roles given to them and the leadership/programming of the Judges, how might the Arisen have turned out?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eugh. You're missing the point of the post, and not quoting the important second paragraph. Treating a bog mummy as like an Arisen without a purpose is fixating on their shared status as real-life preserved corpses and missing the fact that they differ in every other important respect. You may as well create an &quot;Arisen&quot; analogue for every single mortuary custom, because it makes as much sense as focussing only on those that result in (different kinds of) shrunken, withered bodies. They're all as different as each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:41:00-07:00","id":1078078,"title":"","content":"Well, shrunken heads would be a cool Uter relic, like braided onions or garlic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of something substantial to contribute to the thread but I just want to copy/paste what I posted in eight other threads about this topic since the game released half a decade ago, so I'll get back to ya'll","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:03:35-07:00","id":1078095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1077976#post1077976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eugh. You're missing the point of the post, and not quoting the important second paragraph. Treating a bog mummy as like an Arisen without a purpose is fixating on their shared status as real-life preserved corpses and missing the fact that they differ in every other important respect. You may as well create an &quot;Arisen&quot; analogue for every single mortuary custom, because it makes as much sense as focussing only on those that result in (different kinds of) shrunken, withered bodies. They're all as different as each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so we don't treat a bog mummy like an Arisen. What should we treat it like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:11:50-07:00","id":1078105,"title":"","content":"I actually quite like the idea of every mortuary custom having it's own Arisan, or at least having that be what the different types are based on.<br /> <br /> Having a deathless that is reborn as a fiery spirit possessing burnt ashes, or a rotten thing that lives deep beneath the earth, or a wild creature that's god of the wilderness it was left in could be interesting, and could help avoid both having them seem too much like just changing the words in mummy and accidentally othering cultures who actually make mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:28:16-07:00","id":1078111,"title":"","content":"I like that enthusiasm, but are there purposes behind the returns of these beings? An otherworldly force may have enabled their return, but what purpose did their preparers have in mind? What makes these beings live again, as opposed to just being examples of the walking dead and willful spooks? The Mummy core book did have some great rules for revenants, so why are these creatures we're creating here <i>more</i> than mere embodied ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 04-13-2017, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:59:07-07:00","id":1078130,"title":"","content":"So, as far as we can tell the chief difference between an Arisan and just an undead is that A. The arisen have some kind of connection to and control over Sekhem and B. The arisen serve Gods in some direct way.<br /> <br /> If the rite of return was performed in other places at other times, it was presumably for the same reason- to create powerful servants by killing mortals and rebuilding them as vessels for the divine.<br /> The differences would come in A. what kinds of bodies they can return in and the practical effects of that, B. what gods they actuall serve and what they demand and C. What effects their old culture would have on the way they were raised.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, would be thinking like the lesser vampires in Wicked Dead. They;d use the same ruleset- Sekhem, Pillars, returning from death, utterences and affinities, the decent- but in different ways<br /> <br /> For example- the Judges are forces of control, punishment and tyranny, created to cement the rulership of an empire. The Decived were only slightly different, serving the Tekhem (? I don't have the spelling on me) as works of art, immortality vessels and, later, instruments of vengeance. The Shasushken were created as sacrifices pledged to the abstract concept of destruction and decay. The three groups use the same basic mechanics and are, on some level, &quot;the same type of thing&quot;, but they are very different from each other.<br /> <br /> The other types of arisen would be made on a similar level. What about creatures creates to serve dark forces as the last act of vengeance by a dying culture? Or perfect warriors created to promote the rise of an empire and serving elemntal forces of destruction? Or philosopher-angels ensuring the knowledge their home nation found lasts forever in the service of the lords of the Astral? They could be very unique while still mechanically being clearly &quot;the same type of thing&quot; created by the rite of return","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T23:35:04-07:00","id":1078195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078095#post1078095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so we don't treat a bog mummy like an Arisen. What should we treat it like?</div> </div> </div> </div>If not a Revenant, you could just go for an entirely new splat? Beyond being undead there's no connection between the two. Which is why I think trying to parallel the Arisen set-up would be a terrible mistake, and why ultimately why I feel this is a bad sub-forum for this discussion. There's no meaningful reason for a bog mummy to have any more relationship to an Arisen as it would have to a vampire or a Sin Eater. Using Sekhem feels like a mistake, because that suggests an assumption that all preserved corpses come from cultures that manipulate Sekhem and that you have just gotten hung up on the word &quot;Mummy&quot; meaning similar things for different cultures. I feel like a General Discussion thread along the lines of &quot;Let's come up with different undead horrors&quot; may actually do quite well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:28:00-07:00","id":1078256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078195#post1078195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not a Revenant, you could just go for an entirely new splat? Beyond being undead there's no connection between the two. Which is why I think trying to parallel the Arisen set-up would be a terrible mistake, and why ultimately why I feel this is a bad sub-forum for this discussion. There's no meaningful reason for a bog mummy to have any more relationship to an Arisen as it would have to a vampire or a Sin Eater. Using Sekhem feels like a mistake, because that suggests an assumption that all preserved corpses come from cultures that manipulate Sekhem and that you have just gotten hung up on the word &quot;Mummy&quot; meaning similar things for different cultures. I feel like a General Discussion thread along the lines of &quot;Let's come up with different undead horrors&quot; may actually do quite well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True. But this might still have a home here as &quot;let's come up with different Mummy-like undead horrors\u200b, for use in a Mummy game&quot;. We might be able to scavenge some Curse specific mechanics (Affinities, Bane Affinities, Sybaris, Vestiges, etc.) without needing outside references. <br /> <br /> Were it under the general forum, I just feel it should be limited to &quot;Blue Book&quot; terms, or explicitly reference anything that comes from a game-line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-14-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:31:36-07:00","id":1078257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078256#post1078256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. But this might still have a home here as &quot;let's come up with different Mummy-like undead horror, for use in a Mummy game&quot;. We might be able to scavenge some Curse specific mechanics (Affinities, Bane Affinities, Sybaris, Vestiges, etc.) without needing outside references.<br /> <br /> Were it under the general forum, I just feel it should be limited to &quot;Blue Book&quot; terms, or explicitly reference anything that comes from a game-line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, I would prefer no scavenging took place because the conflating of different customs into being supernaturally equivalent due to the English language using the same word for their end product is precisely what I'm finding problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T04:24:06-07:00","id":1078268,"title":"","content":"Anyone that wants non-Iremite mummies has to ask themselves, &quot;Why?&quot; initially. What is it you're even looking for and wanting?<br /> <br /> There's plenty of types of undead in the Chronicles of Darkness. Who's to say a bastardized attempt at the Rite doesn't produce Mekhet vampires, Osiran Prometheans, or Bound who are merged with cthonians rather than Geists? Or just a 'standard' zombie dressed up in tattered desert garb? Or one of the Immortals from that book? Or maybe they're mechanically simply just Shuankhsen, or narratively if your setting is particularly inhospitable.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is all stuff I've said before, and it's coming from someone who would <i>love</i> to see non-Iremite mummies in something like a Night Horrors book for the gameline. Unfortunately, it's really hard for me to come up with a compelling reason to include them into the setting when the above options are just fine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T05:17:07-07:00","id":1078278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078268#post1078268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone that wants non-Iremite mummies has to ask themselves, &quot;Why?&quot; initially. What is it you're even looking for and wanting?<br /> <br /> There's plenty of types of undead in the Chronicles of Darkness. Who's to say a bastardized attempt at the Rite doesn't produce Mekhet vampires, Osiran Prometheans, or Bound who are merged with cthonians rather than Geists? Or just a 'standard' zombie dressed up in tattered desert garb? Or one of the Immortals from that book? Or maybe they're mechanically simply just Shuankhsen, or narratively if your setting is particularly inhospitable.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is all stuff I've said before, and it's coming from someone who would <i>love</i> to see non-Iremite mummies in something like a Night Horrors book for the gameline. Unfortunately, it's really hard for me to come up with a compelling reason to include them into the setting when the above options are just fine</div> </div> </div> </div>Said options are fine, but why not see what we can do to diversify or add to them a bit more? What about basically-ghost!Revenants brought back by Closed Rites and infused with Sekhem that display common Relic-like abilities? Eternals that wake on a cycle and may have Affinities (or even Bane Affinities)? Human-seeming pseudo-Amkhata? Task-bound Ghost-Claimed (but longer lasting) Terracotta warriors... that yearn to be free of their servitude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T05:56:20-07:00","id":1078290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078278#post1078278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Said options are fine, but why not see what we can do to diversify or add to them a bit more? What about basically-ghost!Revenants brought back by Closed Rites and infused with Sekhem that display common Relic-like abilities? Eternals that wake on a cycle and may have Affinities (or even Bane Affinities)? Human-seeming pseudo-Amkhata? Task-bound Ghost-Claimed (but longer lasting) Terracotta warriors... that yearn to be free of their servitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about them? We either have rules for them (Revenants plus Closed Rites and/or Revenants possessing Uter, various experimental Amkhata and Bane Relic infused Amkhata are found in the Avarice Chronicles and other SAS), or they run contrary to the themes of Mummy (Affinities are, after all, programs encoded into the Arisen by the Shan'iatu themselves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:13:19-07:00","id":1078295,"title":"","content":"I've always thought about translating the Cabiri from Resurrection as an example for a bastardized version of the Rite of Return. You know, some weird beings created by sorcerers which tried to achieve immortality by investigating the Arisen, only to get a poor reflection of the Rite's true power and getting hunted by the Judges and their earthly agents.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;why&quot; to have non-Iremite mummies, it is for a number of reasons: first, to emphasis that Sekhem is a global force of nature- after all, if it is a global force of nature, other cultures or beings should have found exotic ways to manipulate it, including creating all kind of undead/deathless/lifeless/other abominations. Second, it is to give mummies something to deal in its own cosmology- vampires shouldn't depend of the Tremere from Mage to have as magical antagonists, and Demon shouldn't depend on the qashmalim as agents of unseen, divine power. The different gamelines are able to crossover with each each other, but each should still function on its own. Just as Mummy's sorcerers shouldn't just be Awakening's mages or Second Sight's taumaturges, their own failed replications of the Rite shouldn't be wholly depended on you searching for other gamelines to find new antagonists. And finally, adding non-Iremtie mummies would make the game feel much wider- it shows that the Arisen's world view is not set on stone, and that are things they can't really explain. This is why it is such a great material for Night Horrors- as one of the recurring themes in those books is things which not only threat the protagonists physically, but also endanger their world view. They don't know anything, even in their own area of expertise. Things which are familiar to them, yet they bend- or even break- the rules of everything they know about reality. It is a wide world out there, and even if you think about yourself as a god king, even the gods could be horrified from looking at that darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:27:34-07:00","id":1078302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078290#post1078290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about them? We either have rules for them (Revenants plus Closed Rites and/or Revenants possessing Uter, various experimental Amkhata and Bane Relic infused Amkhata are found in the Avarice Chronicles and other SAS), or they run contrary to the themes of Mummy (Affinities are, after all, programs encoded into the Arisen by the Shan'iatu themselves).</div> </div> </div> </div>And what books and/or page numbers are such beings detailed in? My point is fleshing out examples, and giving them more background. After all, much of what is in Night Horrors books could just be done with the options already available, yet they are listed.<br /> <br /> As for Affinities:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy: the Curse page 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arisen <b>believe</b> the capacity to manifest these so-called Affinities to have been built directly into the Rite of Return, empowering them with the tools needed to fulfill their intended purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis added. Who says they are correct in their Belief? What stories might be investigated if Affinities were not created by the Shan'iatu, but merely utilized?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:52:15-07:00","id":1078311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078278#post1078278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about basically-ghost!Revenants brought back by Closed Rites and infused with Sekhem that display common Relic-like abilities? Eternals that wake on a cycle and may have Affinities (or even Bane Affinities)? Human-seeming pseudo-Amkhata? Task-bound Ghost-Claimed (but longer lasting) Terracotta warriors... that yearn to be free of their servitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for about half these options you'll find an answer in utilizing Sadikh more. Then you literally just suggested [what might as well be] a Sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Beyond that? Yeah, I think an amkhat stitched together from human flesh would be pretty cool. It's similar to some other ideas I've used, but don't want to talk about at the moment because reasons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:02:49-07:00","id":1078318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078311#post1078311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for about half these options you'll find an answer in utilizing Sadikh more. Then you literally just suggested [what might as well be] a Sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Beyond that? Yeah, I think an amkhat stitched together from human flesh would be pretty cool. It's similar to some other ideas I've used, but don't want to talk about at the moment because reasons</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Sadikh require an Arisen master. Their source and entire existence is based around said Arisen. If you see an active Sadikh, there is an awake Arisen. These would not be thus bound, and could exist independently.<br /> <br /> The Task-bound Terracotta warrior wouldn't be a Sin-Eater due to A) The body isn't alive B) They aren't free, like Sin-Eater presumably are C) They don't really fit Promethean's themes at all either. They exist as something that seems close enough to the Arisen if you lack a lot of information, and present a mirror to the Arisen's own servitude (for them to answer as their faith, or lack of it, in the Judges dictate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Elaboration 04-14-2017, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:04:31-07:00","id":1078321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078295#post1078295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;why&quot; to have non-Iremite mummies, it is for a number of reasons: first, to emphasis that Sekhem is a global force of nature- after all, if it is a global force of nature, other cultures or beings should have found exotic ways to manipulate it, including creating all kind of undead/deathless/lifeless/other abominations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This bugs the ever living heck out of me. Every culture on the planet makes Relics. Not every culture had Shan'iatu desperate to achieve godhood through the usurpation of the underworld with the aid of the manifestation of entropy. It took a specific confluence of events, ambitions, and inhuman power to lead to the creation of the Arisen even being attempted.<br /> <br /> Mummies are not the &quot;baseline&quot; component of their own cosmology. They are the exceptional, the weird, highly specific creation that arose from a corner-case application of Sekhem's metaphysics. If it weren't for the fact that playing as inanimate objects is difficult to pull off, they would be more likely to feature in the Night Horrors book for Relics: The Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078295#post1078295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, it is to give mummies something to deal in its own cosmology- vampires shouldn't depend of the Tremere from Mage to have as magical antagonists, and Demon shouldn't depend on the qashmalim as agents of unseen, divine power. The different gamelines are able to crossover with each each other, but each should still function on its own. Just as Mummy's sorcerers shouldn't just be Awakening's mages or Second Sight's taumaturges, their own failed replications of the Rite shouldn't be wholly depended on you searching for other gamelines to find new antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, after Book of the Deceived came out, I ran Sekhem Sorcerers as the creators and/or wielders of particularly arcane Seba. Before that I did much the same but for specific relics (e.g. an Amulet that grants Telekinesis). Similarly, I have used the Revenant rules printed in the Mummy Core Book to create an array of different undead. Notably, if you combine Old Age, Lucid Dead, Stolen Pillars, Regeneration, and Revenant or Intruder together you end up with a being that very closely mimics a weak Mummy, again within Mummy's existing cosmology.<br /> <br /> But that aside, the idea that Mummies are lacking in things to deal with internally is pretty laughable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078295#post1078295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, adding non-Iremtie mummies would make the game feel much wider- it shows that the Arisen's world view is not set on stone, and that are things they can't really explain. This is why it is such a great material for Night Horrors- as one of the recurring themes in those books is things which not only threat the protagonists physically, but also endanger their world view. They don't know anything, even in their own area of expertise. Things which are familiar to them, yet they bend- or even break- the rules of everything they know about reality. It is a wide world out there, and even if you think about yourself as a god king, even the gods could be horrified from looking at that darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. Non-Iremite Mummies would make the game feel a lot wider. I've been railing against that very idea. Mummy is situated within an extremely confined cultural context for what I consider to be very good reasons. Trying to broaden the game by plastering a new coat of cultural paint onto an idea rooted in the specifically Egyptian variant of mortuary culture makes me supremely uncomfortable. And this fixation on non-Egyptian mummies as the specific medium through which to achieve this &quot;widening&quot; of the game never fails to strike me as weird, when they relate as much to Arisen as an urn full of cremated ash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078302#post1078302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what books and/or page numbers are such beings detailed in? My point is fleshing out examples, and giving them more background. After all, much of what is in Night Horrors books could just be done with the options already available, yet they are listed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mummy Core book, by and large. Specifically the section on the Dead, but I can't remember the page numbers from the top of my head.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078302#post1078302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Affinities:<br /> <br /> <br /> Emphasis added. Who says they are correct in their Belief? What stories might be investigated if Affinities were not created by the Shan'iatu, but merely utilized?</div> </div> </div> </div>When Book of the Deceived came out there were a few arguments from people clinging to pet fan theories who used the unreliable narrator of that book's main lore dump as an excuse to discount the more troublesome components, for them, of that book's mythology. That's fine in your own game, but unreliable or not the game writers write words in books for more reasons than for players to look at them and go, &quot;Nah, probably a lie&quot; (exceptions exist, usually for obvious discrepancies). If the Arisen believe a piece of information, and we have no contrary information to it, then I'm inclined to think that they are correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:16:39-07:00","id":1078330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078195#post1078195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I think trying to parallel the Arisen set-up would be a terrible mistake, and why ultimately why I feel this is a bad sub-forum for this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, but since the moderators have said this is the last chance for a thread like this, please could we dispense with the usual round of arguing over whether it should exist?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078295#post1078295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;why&quot; to have non-Iremite mummies, it is for a number of reasons: first, to emphasis that Sekhem is a global force of nature- after all, if it is a global force of nature, other cultures or beings should have found exotic ways to manipulate it, including creating all kind of undead/deathless/lifeless/other abominations. Second, it is to give mummies something to deal in its own cosmology- vampires shouldn't depend of the Tremere from Mage to have as magical antagonists, and Demon shouldn't depend on the qashmalim as agents of unseen, divine power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Mummy is a game where the main protagonists spend a lot of time &quot;off,&quot; while the world stubbornly insists on having things happen without them. New manipulations of Sekhem should definitely factor into that.<br /> <br /> However, I think the common thread should be &quot;manipulations of Sekhem,&quot; rather than mummies per se - if it produces mummies of a sort, it's not because the sorcerers in question necessarily wanted mummies, but because mummification is a necessary component of Sekhem-fulled immortality (fitting for a magical force that draws little distinction between spirituality and materiality). More cultures would be producing relics outside the remits of the five Guilds than are producing mummies that are neither Deathless nor Lifeless - and of course non-walking-around mummies make pretty good uter.<br /> <br /> For mummies themselves, the first question is why? As in what is the purpose of their immortality? For Andean mallqui, this is likely to be some combination of serving as an ancestral focus or serving as messenger between the divine and the Earth - which in game terms would shake out pretty well to what the Arisen do for their cults - but as an end, rather than a means. For those hard core Buddhist monks who mummified themselves, the point would be a search for enlightenment. If any later Egyptian mummies were intended to walk around, it was probably just to protect themselves.<br /> (In contrast, I think if the Pazyrik Ice Maiden or the Lindow Man got up one day, they <i>should</i> be revenants rather than quasi-Arisen).<br /> <br /> What they have or don't have can follow from that.<br /> <br /> Mallqui under this model could be summoned up by their communities into something pretty much like a Descent cycle (though the things that hasten or slow it might be different). If their function is to help their communities, I'd give them something like Kepher senses, but applying to the problem their people are facing rather than relics. Since they weren't able to prevent the conquest by forces that <i>didn't</i> have mummies, I'd say there aren't many of them - maybe a dozen - and they're not as powerful as the Deathless (let them have Affinities - not necessarily the same ones, but that type of power - but not Utterances). Summoning would also be the only way they can wake up - if their people are gone, the next time they fall asleep will be for good - yes, this means a mallqui will have been created by the cult/community/ayllu it serves.<br /> (This is also the option that would be easiest to generalise into something that's not always mummies. An ancestral ghost that serves as a family genius might be summoned into possession of a family member, accompanied by a burst of Sekhem, for example).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the monks would start off in what the Deathless would consider apotheosis - and may be able to stay awake indefinitely at Sekhem 1, unless some outside party trashes them (which might be a permanent kill). Their numbers would be even lower than for mallqui - perhaps only one or two have ever accomplished this. On the other hand, they could be epic - Himalayan myth credits monks and sages with feats easily comparable to Utterances - but they'd have build up their Skehem for that, somehow, and it would bleed off quickly (think of it as a Descent where you're going against your purpose, with no way to slow it down).<br /> <br /> Like Shuankhsen, I'd give other mummies only one Pillar - or at most two (one derived from personality, one derived from their cultural purpose).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:30:05-07:00","id":1078338,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I do agree that making mummies based on other actual mummification methods would be a bad idea, both for the social justice reasons mentioned and that it seems a bit predictable? I think any alternate deathless should be a bit more unique to the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078321#post1078321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every culture had Shan'iatu desperate to achieve godhood through the usurpation of the underworld with the aid of the manifestation of entropy. It took a specific confluence of events, ambitions, and inhuman power to lead to the creation of the Arisen even being attempted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to disagree. Sure, not every culture had the Shan'itau, but in the world of darkness I bet a lot of them had their own powerful sorcerers who had good reasons to make powerful immortal minions and the amorality to kill thousands to do it.<br /> That's part of why I like the idea of there being more then one- if it can be done in the middle east, it can be done in the rest of the world, and it just seems a little implausible that no-one except Irem <i>ever</i> learnt about the life-force of the universe and thought that perverting it to create magical WMDs might be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:33:19-07:00","id":1078340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078321#post1078321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This bugs the ever living heck out of me. Every culture on the planet makes Relics. Not every culture had Shan'iatu desperate to achieve godhood through the usurpation of the underworld with the aid of the manifestation of entropy. It took a specific confluence of events, ambitions, and inhuman power to lead to the creation of the Arisen even being attempted.<br /> <br /> Mummies are not the &quot;baseline&quot; component of their own cosmology. They are the exceptional, the weird, highly specific creation that arose from a corner-case application of Sekhem's metaphysics. If it weren't for the fact that playing as inanimate objects is difficult to pull off, they would be more likely to feature in the Night Horrors book for Relics: The Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, every culture can create Relics, and every culture can make Amkhat, but what about things which are unique to the cultures which birthed them? Other cultures should make their own, unique creations, and give alternative readings to how the cosmology is built. Sekhem should feel wider- but right now, it feels that everything which is important or interesting about it comes from that same desert empire which was drown beneath the sands millenia ago. I want other cultures to make interesting things with Sekhem, and see how it is seen through different eyes. Non iremite Sekhem enhanced beings could be used to advance that view- as why on earth only one culture in the whole world should be the only one to make something exceptional with Sekhem? Why can't other cultures make their own interesting, exceptional, weird and highly specific creations? I'm not saying that every culture on earth should have made Sekhem enhanced beings (I avoid the word mummies because I don't care about them being mummies), but some should have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, after Book of the Deceived came out, I ran Sekhem Sorcerers as the creators and/or wielders of particularly arcane Seba. Before that I did much the same but for specific relics (e.g. an Amulet that grants Telekinesis). Similarly, I have used the Revenant rules printed in the Mummy Core Book to create an array of different undead. Notably, if you combine Old Age, Lucid Dead, Stolen Pillars, Regeneration, and Revenant or Intruder together you end up with a being that very closely mimics a weak Mummy, again within Mummy's existing cosmology.<br /> <br /> But that aside, the idea that Mummies are lacking in things to deal with internally is pretty laughable. </div> </div> </div>I do not understand that argument. I haven't said that Mummy lacks antagonists. I've said that a concept that comes from Mummy should use Mummy's rules. The concept of bastardized version of the Rite comes from Mummy, and as such should be used through Mummy's tool box. I have no problem with what you are saying- I have a problem with saying that Mekhet or Osirian are the only example for failed replications of the Rite. I don't understand how giving an example, even unique, antagonist created through a failed attempt to recreate the Rite using the rules for Revenants and their like is a problem of any kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't disagree. Non-Iremite Mummies would make the game feel a lot wider. I've been railing against that very idea. Mummy is situated within an extremely confined cultural context for what I consider to be very good reasons. Trying to broaden the game by plastering a new coat of cultural paint onto an idea rooted in the specifically Egyptian variant of mortuary culture makes me supremely uncomfortable. And this fixation on non-Egyptian mummies as the specific medium through which to achieve this &quot;widening&quot; of the game never fails to strike me as weird, when they relate as much to Arisen as an urn full of cremated ash. </div> </div> </div>Maybe because it is the only gameline which is so specifically tied to a single culture. Maybe because it feels like it gives Egyptian mythology a special treatment which makes it feel weird. Maybe because through variant non Iremite mummies or similar beings, people could see the game from different angles, and not only through egyptian-like eyes.<br /> <br /> Notice- I don't argue that new mummy like beings should be copy-paste of the Arisen with some cultural paint. I argue for the existence of new, Sekhem based lifeforms created by other cultures, be them Lifeless, Deathless, Undead, living, just dead, ephemereal, spiritual, infernal or any other kind of subtitle you would feel comfortable with, which could either be created independently, spontaneously or by people investigating existing rituals and products of Iremite creations. I think that saying &quot;this one culture is the only one that matters as no other had divine help&quot; makes me much more uncomfortable than saying &quot;look, other cultures can make mummies of some kind too!&quot;.<br /> <br /> In sort, I don't want a copy paste of existing Arisen with new aesthetic. I want other cultures to make their own unique creations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:35:01-07:00","id":1078342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078321#post1078321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mummy Core book, by and large. Specifically the section on the Dead, but I can't remember the page numbers from the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just read through the section. It doesn't list any such beings there. It has some Numina (most of which overcome shortcomings of the 1E Ghost template), but no real critters as such. A collection of parts does not a model make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078321#post1078321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Book of the Deceived came out there were a few arguments from people clinging to pet fan theories who used the unreliable narrator of that book's main lore dump as an excuse to discount the more troublesome components, for them, of that book's mythology. That's fine in your own game, but unreliable or not the game writers write words in books for more reasons than for players to look at them and go, &quot;Nah, probably a lie&quot; (exceptions exist, usually for obvious discrepancies). If the Arisen believe a piece of information, and we have no contrary information to it, then I'm inclined to think that they are correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying they are lying. It says &quot;The Arisen believe&quot;. I think that is true. It <b>doesn't</b> say that Affinities are, for a fact, built into the Rite, merely that the Arisen believe that to be true. And I think they are right, the Arisen do believe that. But beliefs can be incorrect. If they said &quot;Affinities are built directly into the Rite of Return&quot;, that would be different, but I think they chose the ambiguity of &quot;The Arisen believe&quot; as a qualifier for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T10:42:11-07:00","id":1078420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078340#post1078340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yes, every culture can create Relics..(words words words)...I want other cultures to make their own unique creations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post, forever. I tried to make these points back in the second thread, with analogies likening the Shan'iatu's actions to setting off a mystical atom bomb, with anomalous entities a result of the 'fallout', but LostLight explains it here just <i>so much better</i>I<br /> <br /> So, let us continue with this premise, which unless I am very much misreading it here, is 'Sekhem will find a way' (with apologies to Jeff Goldblum and Michael Crichton).<br /> <br /> Now it has been pointed out that the Rite of Return required a truly massive amount of resources to pull off, but why? How much of it was actually necessary, and how much was alternately a tithe to Ammut for its help, or just plain old trial and error? Even leaving Fate (i.e., Storyteller/Player Fiat) out of the equation, what would be needed for an appropriate amount of Sekhem to infuse a body to bring it back, if not as Arisen, then as something sufficiently similar for our purposes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:15:13-07:00","id":1078429,"title":"","content":"I would say if you are creating something on the level of the arisen, probably a lot of death. They are probably the most powerful entity type in the WoD (barring maybe demons and high-level mages), and you'd need a lot of power to make one, and it looks like Sekhem (to use the iremite term- the other groups probably have their own names) mostly comes from releasing it by killing things.<br /> <br /> Although I guess there could be other ways. Using the atom bomb analogy, while you need a lot to make a mystic atom bomb, you might be able to get away with using less to make a mystic cruise missle (or even hand grenade- imagine a group that made tens of thousands of minor deathless rather then a few hundred big ones. An army of Shuankshen in the mountains, just waiting for someone to wake them up...). <br /> <br /> You might also find other sources. A godlike entity could &quot;foot the bill&quot;, although what it would want in exchange might be just as bad as mass-slaughter. Mass ecological destruction might release enough life energy for those who are squeamish about killing humans (fun fact- many geologists think the Sahara was a lush area only 10,000 years ago). An immortal logically has more Sekhem then a normal human, as might rapidly healing creatures like werewolves or prometheans. I'm imagining a conspiracy who hunts monsters to fuel their modern day rite of return.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can get Sekhem in huge amounts from the relics, cities and even bodies of those who already use it. Say, what <i>did</i> happen to the Nameless Empire in the end, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:00:09-07:00","id":1078607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078429#post1078429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I guess there could be other ways. Using the atom bomb analogy, while you need a lot to make a mystic atom bomb, you might be able to get away with using less to make a mystic cruise missle (or even hand grenade- imagine a group that made tens of thousands of minor deathless rather then a few hundred big ones. An army of Shuankshen in the mountains, just waiting for someone to wake them up...).</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, in my analogy the atom bomb was the act of rewiring the cosmos to allow beings like the Arisen to exist in the first place, not just beings of their power level, so your &quot;arms race&quot; take on it kind of falls flat for me. That said, I think you're right that it would take less energy to repeat the process, but again, how much of what was sacrificed was actually <i>necessary</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:32:52-07:00","id":1078628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078340#post1078340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that saying &quot;this one culture is the only one that matters as no other had divine help&quot; makes me much more uncomfortable than saying &quot;look, other cultures can make mummies of some kind too!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since when you add Last Dynasty International to the mix, it kinda becomes &quot;this ancient culture with divine help and modern white people.&quot; But anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In sort, I don't want a copy paste of existing Arisen with new aesthetic. I want other cultures to make their own unique creations. </div> </div> </div>One option that I don't think has been considered is using the different Great Crafts to create analogous achievements to the Deathless. Say the Deathless themselves aren't just works of necromancy, but also works of <i>uter</i> in the relic sense of the word. The Shan'iatu were already great necromancers, and incorporated it into Rite of Return for the sake of efficiency (and maybe because they had just enough heart to allow their servants to keep at least their bodies for themselves) - and that is why the Sahu forms around the mummified body - another reason to do it the easy way would be that the Shan'iatu were doing some other pretty sustantial magics at the same time.<br /> <br /> But it's not impossible for the Sahu to form independently of the Deathless-alike's material tie. Going back to the Andean mallqui, mummies were often wrapped up in bundles of cloth, along with other goods - and &quot;textile&quot; is sure as hell a fitting class of relic for the Andes. So maybe it's the bundle that's the important thing, not the corpse per se - supernatural mallqui rest inside them when it whatever they have in place of henet, but when called to action form a body apart from the mummy bundle - they have a greater tie to the Sekhem of their communities than the Arisen would have to their cults, which might be what makes that possible. That way, a mallqui's physical mummy would be more analogous to an Arisen's Tomb (balancing being easier to move with worse consequences for damaging it).<br /> <br /> Further afield:<br /> <br /> Amulets by nature implant knowledge and proclivities - which gives them tremendous vehicle for possession. Could the souls of a person be taken and physically shaped into a small object as the carrier for their Sekhem?<br /> <br /> Effigies are larger figures and works of architecture - and more than other relics, they display what can almost be called agendas. Could a version of the Rite bring someone back as an ushabti, or write them into a building or earthwork as a genius loci?<br /> <br /> Regia are a bit more difficult. The key element - the bit that would have to be emphasised as a work of Sekhem - is more process than object. How would that manifest?<br /> <br /> Texts are back to the simple - writing souls into texts is a trope thats been around since writing began, most likely. Instead of their mummies, later Egyptian Deathless might have lived in their funerary texts. Could they make temporary bodies, or influence the people who read them? Would you have the King in Yellow as a PC?<br /> <br /> Seba - becoming a living idea - could be the ultimate in apotheosis. Or even Apotheosis. Those hard-core monks I mentioned might become enlightenment itself, only making new bodies when they need them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:58:59-07:00","id":1078640,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of an Text Deathless that takes the form of one of the curses you find on gravesites- you read it and laugh, not knowing the tomb's guardian has already Arisen inside your head.<br /> <br /> For a Regia deathless, maybe some kind of object or machine that builds a body for the soul out of whatever material is around. Each time it wakes up, it might be something radically different depending on where the device was activated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:01:14-07:00","id":1078641,"title":"","content":"These are some intriguing ideas; I'm already thinking of the Genius Loci mummy who can have their Cult 'summon' a physical form for them in their Temple-Body, but whose life force is bound there; they can go explore the world, but only there can their 'body' be healed.<br /> <br /> Also, a thought on Regia: have you considered concepts like herbalism and internal alchemy? If the Arisen are essentially Revenents+, then these fellows could be Purified+.<br /> <br /> As great as these alternate-crafts Arisen ideas are, and as much insight as they provide in giving us new ways to look at the Curse, they could still conceivably be products of Irem, so I think they would work better in their own thread,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 04-14-2017, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:21:41-07:00","id":1078655,"title":"","content":"So they don't die first, but perfect the processes inside them to become immortal? That would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:54:39-07:00","id":1078700,"title":"","content":"For the purposes of continuing this thought experiment, let's say that it takes 100 deaths to create one Deathless, barring any external factors (experimentation, patrons to appease, etc.). Outside of mass sacrifice/execution (&quot;The Irem Method&quot;), how can this number be achieved? Right off the top of my head, I'm thinking of plague, or some sort of natural disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T19:03:41-07:00","id":1078705,"title":"","content":"A war would be the obvious choice. If you had some way of storing sekhem, serial murder could count- it would take a while but you could maybe do it without people noticing you were making an abomination. If you're subtle AND powerful, poverty and famine could get the deaths without anyone being able to trace it back to you. For a modern day group, criminal negligence might even work- put out a product with dangerous side effects, wait for the numbers to rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":".  Sekhem and Irem are two different things, what'dya know? 04-14-2017, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T00:18:11-07:00","id":1078793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078338#post1078338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, not every culture had the Shan'itau, but in the world of darkness I bet a lot of them had their own powerful sorcerers who had good reasons to make powerful immortal minions and the amorality to kill thousands to do it.<br /> That's part of why I like the idea of there being more then one- <b>if it can be done in the middle east, it can be done in the rest of the world</b>, and it just seems a little implausible that no-one except Irem <i>ever</i> learnt about the life-force of the universe and thought that perverting it to create magical WMDs might be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core book literally says it <i>can't</i>. It states the Rite of Return was the single greatest spell ever performed. It wrote an empire out of history, reworked the fabric of the cosmos, and was preceded by the death of a <i>god</i>, all carried out by traitorous, otherworldly divine spirits, not 'just' arch-mages.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm sorry. I'm not trying to stamp out good ideas or attempts at expanding the setting - just the ones that <i>directly contradict core material</i>.<br /> <br /> The game has plenty of room for other cultures manipulating Sekhem (even though Dark Eras compares it to the equivalent of handling nuclear radiation with your bare hands in the section talking about Awakened mages), strange and unknowable ghosts, sanity-shattering demons, and varieties of immortals (which is why <i>I</i> added that crossover section to the Dark Eras Companion section). I'd argue it has room for 'lesser' non-Iremite mummies, too, but it's very difficult to include any that don't undermine Iremite mythology or wouldn't be better covered by the themes of the Arisen, Deceived, Shuankhsen, or Sadikh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T01:02:58-07:00","id":1078800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078628#post1078628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since when you add Last Dynasty International to the mix, it kinda becomes &quot;this ancient culture with divine help and modern white people.&quot; But anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a vast overestimation of what Last Dynasty's harvesting of stolen life force actually equates to. It isn't anything even remotely on par with Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 04-15-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T06:21:00-07:00","id":1078854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078793#post1078793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book literally says it <i>can't</i>. It states the Rite of Return was the single greatest spell ever performed. It wrote an empire out of history, reworked the fabric of the cosmos, and was preceded by the death of a <i>god</i>, all carried out by traitorous, otherworldly divine spirits, not 'just' arch-mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, that part about writing an empire out of history and reworking the fabric of the cosmos were <i>what the Shan'iatu wanted to do</i> - those things, not making the Deathless as a support mechanism, are the reason it's the greatest spell ever performed. If later sorcerers figure out how to make a few Sekhem-infused undying beings, that's comparative child's play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T07:44:18-07:00","id":1078886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1078793#post1078793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book literally says it <i>can't</i>. It states the Rite of Return was the single greatest spell ever performed. It wrote an empire out of history, reworked the fabric of the cosmos, and was preceded by the death of a <i>god</i>, all carried out by traitorous, otherworldly divine spirits, not 'just' arch-mages.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm sorry. I'm not trying to stamp out good ideas or attempts at expanding the setting - just the ones that <i>directly contradict core material</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly why I've been exploring the 'unintended consequences' angle; it's much easier to align with existing canon.<br /> <br /> Also, you wrote the Immortals crossover material? Very nice! Though I am curious as to why the Purified were notably absent...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:06:44-07:00","id":1078891,"title":"","content":"I didn't write it, but I asked for it and Matthew Dawkins wrote it up. I personally don't like the Purified, and - surprise - thought there was unnecessary thematic overlap regarding their inclusion.<br /> <br /> As far as 'unintended consequences' go, that's why we created the Legio. I wanted to - surprise - expand the setting with sanity-shattering (not so much?) ghost-demons trapped in Twilight and composed of many shattered individuals, and the same writer nailed it when he described them as being more uncounted victims of the Rite. That may not soothe you since they're still Iremite in origin, but at the same time it lays out precedent for the very ideas you want to create.<br /> <br /> So we don't totally agree on everything but I did my part in initiating content I thought was appropriate, and Mattew did a bang up job in making my money worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T10:24:36-07:00","id":1078947,"title":"","content":"Wait, there's immortals crossover material? no-one told me about this, no-one told be about the dark age companion, grumble grumble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:43:32-07:00","id":1080127,"title":"","content":"OK, hope everyone had a good holiday. Now, back to work!<br /> <br /> I believe that someone mentioned monks who effectively self-mummified themselves? That sounds like an interesting avenue to explore; does anyone have more information on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:02:44-07:00","id":1080430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080127#post1080127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that someone mentioned monks who effectively self-mummified themselves? That sounds like an interesting avenue to explore; does anyone have more information on that?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sokushinbutsu\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> is the top link I found on the subject, though I first heard about it in the context of the Himalayas. The forensic analysis dovetailed with the process described in the article. As it notes, few monks who attempted it actually succeeded, and it would be reasonable to assume if this can result in a supernatural mummy, only one or two have ever managed it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:31:18-07:00","id":1080627,"title":"","content":"OK, the article says that this type of self-mummification was for reaching new levels of enlightenment. In my mind's eye, I see them succeeding, and encountering...something, a Shan'iatu analog (Hell, at this point we might as well call it 'ShenLong'). Guarding the secrets of immortality (amongst other things), it accepts the self-made as its agents. <br /> <br /> Now, let's set mechanics aside for a moment; Who would the main enemies of the self-made be, their Shuankhsen/Deceived? My first thought was to go the 'Wicked Emperor and his Immortal Guard', but that seemed a bit too cliche. Anyone have any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T17:28:32-07:00","id":1080655,"title":"","content":"If we are going with &quot;enlightenment and truth&quot; as their reason for being created, then &quot;lies&quot; is the obvious thing. Maybe those too impure for enlightenment, cast back down to earth but with enough Sekhem to become something, not quite immortal and not quite able to die, eternally racked with envy over what they were denied.<br /> <br /> It can be a more black and white compared to the more justifiable Shuankhsen/Deceived. Alternately, given that the beings behind these arisen are still the Shan'itau, notable for having hypocritical and arbitrary laws and being proud of it, the standards of &quot;enlightenment&quot; aren't necessarily what Buddhism sees as good traits.<br /> <br /> Kindly and faithful monks, cast out of heaven on the arbitrary whims of a monster, trapped in a body unable to reincarnate and always watching their crueller compatriots enjoy the gifts of immortality in the name of a faith they endlessly pervert- there's some story potential in there, at least.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T17:55:01-07:00","id":1080663,"title":"","content":"Some demon king of deception (read: agent of Ammut)?<br /> <br /> Would they be built like Apotheosis mummies? More Affinities (mechanically) representing Enlightened techniques, less Utterances? Hmm, a bit crossover-y, but what about using Wisdom instead of Memory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:47:13-07:00","id":1080690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080655#post1080655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are going with &quot;enlightenment and truth&quot; as their reason for being created, then &quot;lies&quot; is the obvious thing. Maybe those too impure for enlightenment, cast back down to earth but with enough Sekhem to become something, not quite immortal and not quite able to die, eternally racked with envy over what they were denied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get the 'truth' bit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be a more black and white compared to the more justifiable Shuankhsen/Deceived. Alternately, given that the beings behind these arisen are still the Shan'itau, notable for having hypocritical and arbitrary laws and being proud of it, the standards of &quot;enlightenment&quot; aren't necessarily what Buddhism sees as good traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>ShenLong <i>isn't</i> the Shan'iatu; they just fill roughly the same cosmological niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindly and faithful monks, cast out of heaven on the arbitrary whims of a monster, trapped in a body unable to reincarnate and always watching their crueller compatriots enjoy the gifts of immortality in the name of a faith they endlessly pervert- there's some story potential in there, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the whole &quot;perverted faith&quot; bit, but the cast-out-of-heaven-for-the-actions-of-others part; assuming that ShenLong is a stern, Legalist-style entity, this could work very well., especially if the &quot;impure ones&quot; (I'm looking back at my Emperor/Guard idea) effectively stole the secrets of immortality from the self-made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:04:25-07:00","id":1080698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080690#post1080690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get the 'truth' bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enlightenment is truth, and the understanding of truths. To reach enlightenment, you must understand truths and escape lies. It's the most basic aspect of it, and it would be weird to ignore it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080690#post1080690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ShenLong <i>isn't</i> the Shan'iatu; they just fill roughly the same cosmological niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was working on the assumption that it was, if not the same being, the same kind of being and thus somewhat subject to the same rules. What do you mean by the same cosmolgical niche- another servant of the judges? An equal to the judges? An unrelated creature that just happens to control sekhem too?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080690#post1080690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know about the whole &quot;perverted faith&quot; bit, but the cast-out-of-heaven-for-the-actions-of-others part; assuming that ShenLong is a stern, Legalist-style entity, this could work very well., especially if the &quot;impure ones&quot; (I'm looking back at my Emperor/Guard idea) effectively stole the secrets of immortality from the self-made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, my idea has some acceptence! Maybe they tried to follow the ritual. Or maybe they were stolen from- they did the ritual <i>first. </i>and the later group were better servants, leading to the orignals being cast out. That would lead to a lot of resentment and a desire to reclaim their place, or at least cause the Deathless to fall too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":".  I am not good at html apparently 04-18-2017, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:24:26-07:00","id":1080702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080698#post1080698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enlightenment is truth, and the understanding of truths. To reach enlightenment, you must understand truths and escape lies. It's the most basic aspect of it, and it would be weird to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but the truth/lies dichotomy doesn't have any great bearing on the nature of the self-mades' adversaries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, I was working on the assumption that it was, if not the same being, the same kind of being and thus somewhat subject to the same rules. What do you mean by the same cosmolgical niche- another servant of the judges? An equal to the judges? An unrelated creature that just happens to control sekhem too? </div> </div> </div>The last one, though it doesn't &quot;control Sekhem&quot; any more than the Shan'iatu do (at best, they're both very good at influencing it); ShenLong exists, the self-made encounter it, and it lets them stay in the Heavenly Realms if they agree to do certain jobs for it. If they don't, then they are stuck in the Earthly Realm, unable to restore their personal energy and so are limited to resurrect with the bare minimum of energy (come back with Sekhem 1).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yay, my idea has some acceptence! Maybe they tried to follow the ritual. Or maybe they were stolen from- they did the ritual <i>first. </i>and the later group were better servants, leading to the orignals being cast out. That would lead to a lot of resentment and a desire to reclaim their place, or at least cause the Deathless to fall too. </div> </div> </div> If we use the Emperor/Guard conceit, then perhaps they forced immortality (wicked alchemy or whatnot), using sorcery to try an <i>take</i> what should be <i>earned</i> (or at least, that's how ShenLong sees it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:28:56-07:00","id":1080704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1080663#post1080663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some demon king of deception (read: agent of Ammut)?<br /> <br /> Would they be built like Apotheosis mummies? More Affinities (mechanically) representing Enlightened techniques, less Utterances? Hmm, a bit crossover-y, but what about using Wisdom instead of Memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd stick with Memory, but have it not represent memories of past Descents so much as past existence in the Heavenly Realms; it would have similar functions as Memory for Apothesized Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:51:37-07:00","id":1082436,"title":"","content":"OK, new hypothetical for our self-made: Their general purpose in the world. As self-initiated immortals, they have no pre-planned instructions from the outset but have 'missions' assigned by the Legalistic Sekhem Force governing their continued existence in the Heavenly Realms. These missions center around maintaining the smooth flow of Sekhem throughout the world, which can range from the 'processing' (draining) of Relics, slaying Amkhata (or whatever Asiatic variations thereof exist) and other Lifeless beings, and even geomantic landscaping to &quot;smooth out&quot; existing Sekhem flows. Needless to say, a number of these actions can bring them into conflict with the Arisen, but could just as likely bring them in on the same side.<br /> <br /> As always, comments and constructive criticisms are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:16:33-07:00","id":1083433,"title":"","content":"That sounds good to me. Come to think of it, comparisons to Apotheosis have been to what happens when the mainstream Arisen attain it - but in light of what you suggest for their mission, perhaps their state is more akin to what would hypothetically happen to a Deceived getting it and becoming an instrument of Fate. Perhaps for the self-made, both states are attainable, but greater power and cultural idealism accrue to the more Deceived-like version, while concentrating on their own memory (and Memory) is something of a fallen state, both morally (or &quot;morally&quot; and metaphysically - that way, they're kind of their <i>own</i> Shuankhsen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 04-25-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T19:13:03-07:00","id":1084813,"title":"","content":"Morally and metaphysically? How so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T14:01:20-07:00","id":1085132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1077188-on-non-iremite-mummies-v-4-0?p=1084813#post1084813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morally and metaphysically? How so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if their ideal state is to be servants of &quot;the Legalistic Sekhem Force governing their continued existence in the Heavenly Realms&quot; (which I imagine Deceived and Deathless would consider to be Fate), then losing themselves in their own concerns, as with Memory would be a moral failing in their eyes. And it might cost them metaphysical strength to do so as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:48:11-07:00","id":1085287,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I meant the LSF to be more of a Judge-like entity, but a pre-existing one, rather than self-elevated like the shan'iatu. Memory wouldn't be discouraged (at least not to the same degree it is by the Judges), but the main concern would be Right Action.<br /> <br /> And serving the LSF wouldn't necessarily be an ideal state (though individual self-initiated may view it as such), but more like accepting patronage in exchange for performing tasks. They are free to return to the World without accepting the LSF's offer, but their existence becomes similar to a Shuankhsen's, Sekhem-wise: they return with minimal Sekhem recovery, as opposed to a servant's &quot;full charge&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T10:20:32-07:00","id":1091191,"title":"","content":"Alright, so far for our new mummies we have sketched out<br /> <br /> 1). an origin (self-initiated immortals, ranging from self-mummified monks to internal alchemists)<br /> 2). A patron, the stern, Legalist Judge of the Dead, Yama (based roughly on the Buddhist deity)<br /> 3). an antagonist force (the Wicked Emperor and his Guard, who sought immortality for worldly power rather than self-knowledge)<br /> 4). a freedom/redemption mechanic (choosing whether or not to serve Yama in the first place; yes gets you an Arisen-style rebirth/Sekhem recharge cycle, while no gets you, at best, being called back by a cult, and at worst, rising by the vagueries of chance, returning with low Sekhem in the Shuankhsen style)<br /> <br /> These being established, I think the next step should be template abilities/powers. What aspects should every member of this new mummy type have? If anyone needs help with ideas, I recommend the Hunter supplement <u>Mortal Remains</u>; the Appendix has an excellent section on Monster template creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}